{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.HeckeGS","@type":"LeanModule","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.HeckeGS","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Basic","lean:module:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.AlgOps","lean:module:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.CompositionLemma","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Logic.Function.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Abel","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.BigOperators.Group.Finset.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Order.BigOperators.Group.Finset"],"declarations":67,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.threading_cost_unique","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.threading_cost_unique","kind":"theorem","line":852,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeGS.lean#L852-L874","doc":"Threading cost uniqueness: two reductions of the same augmented braid\nyield identical normal forms — again **conditionally** on `hgs`, for the\nsame reason as `heckeCost_well_defined`, and again vacuous for this system.\nThe unconditional form is\n`HeckeCompletion.heckeCompleted_threading_cost_unique`. The \"no quasi-zeros\"\nhypothesis is discharged here: `HeckeGen (n+1)` has a generator, so the free\nalgebra on it has none. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.heckeCost_well_defined","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.heckeCost_well_defined","kind":"theorem","line":827,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeGS.lean#L827-L850","doc":"Normal forms of a Hecke algebra element are unique — **conditionally on\nthe system being a GS basis**, which is now an explicit hypothesis rather\nthan the deleted axiom. `NotAGSBasis.hecke_not_gs_basis_four` shows the\nhypothesis is unsatisfiable at `n = 4` for `heckeRewritingSystem` as it\nstands, so this statement is vacuous as it applies to *this* system.\n\nThe Bokut–Shiao completion has since been added and proved:\n`HeckeCompletion.heckeCompleted_normalForm_unique` is this statement against\n`heckeCompletedRewritingSystem`, with the hypothesis discharged. Use that\none; this stays because it is stated at the level the abstract framework\nworks at, and because deleting it would erase the record of why the\nuncompleted system cannot support it. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.heckeCost_nonneg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.heckeCost_nonneg","kind":"theorem","line":819,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeGS.lean#L819-L823","doc":"The Hecke cost is non-negative. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.heckeCost","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.heckeCost","kind":"def","line":810,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeGS.lean#L810-L817","doc":"The Hecke cost of an element: the sum of absolute values of\ncoefficients across the entire support.\n\n`heckeCost(f) = Σ_{m ∈ supp(f)} |f.coeff(m)|`\n\nThis is well-defined because `support` is a `Finset`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.augmentedBraidElement","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.augmentedBraidElement","kind":"def","line":787,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeGS.lean#L787-L806","doc":"The augmented braid element for threading: prepend the photon\nstrand above the hadron, then un-braid below.\n\n`augmentedBraid β_H = σ_n · σ_{n-1} · … · σ₁ · β_H · σ₁⁻¹ · … · σ_n⁻¹`\n\nIn the `B_{n+1}` embedding (generators `σ₀, …, σ_n` indexed by `Fin (n+1)`).\n\n**Corrected 2026-11-15 (bean `qou-078y`).** The photon letters are now\nbuilt as explicit `(i, sign)` pairs. They were written as signed integers\n`-(i : ℤ)`, and for `i = 0` that is `+0`, so the first un-braiding letter\ncame out as the positive `σ₀` instead of `σ₀⁻¹`. The hadron word keeps the\nsigned-integer encoding for its callers; see `decodeSigned`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.braidToAlg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.braidToAlg","kind":"def","line":781,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeGS.lean#L781-L785","doc":"Embed a braid word in the signed-integer encoding (see `decodeSigned`\nfor its `σ₀⁻¹` limitation). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.decodeSigned","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.decodeSigned","kind":"def","line":769,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeGS.lean#L769-L779","doc":"Decode the signed-integer braid encoding: `g ≥ 0` is `σ_{g mod n}`, and\n`g < 0` is `σ_{|g| mod n}⁻¹`.\n\n**Limitation of this encoding.** `-0 = 0`, so `σ₀⁻¹` has no code: the\ninteger `-(0 : ℤ)` decodes to the positive letter `σ₀`. Callers that need\n`σ₀⁻¹` must build letters directly and use `braidLettersToAlg`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.braidLettersToAlg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.braidLettersToAlg","kind":"def","line":742,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeGS.lean#L742-L767","doc":"Embed a braid word given as explicit letters `(i, sign)` into\n`AlgElement`, `true` = `σᵢ`, `false` = `σᵢ⁻¹`, by left-multiplying each\ngenerator's embedding successively: for `[l₁, l₂, l₃]` the value is\n`embed(l₁) · embed(l₂) · embed(l₃)`.\n\nPositive letters are singletons, so the product is `leftMulGen σᵢ`.\nNegative letters are `σᵢ - (q - q⁻¹)`, so the product distributes as\n`σᵢ · acc - (q - q⁻¹) · acc`.\n\n**This is a product in the FREE algebra.** No Hecke relation is applied, so\nthe result is in general not a normal form, and `heckeCost` of it is the\ncost of an unreduced word expansion, not of the Hecke-algebra element. The\nreduced cost is `HeckeReducedCost.IsReducedCost`, which takes the normal\nform in the completed system first. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.embedGenerator","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.embedGenerator","kind":"def","line":729,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeGS.lean#L729-L740","doc":"Embed a signed braid generator into `AlgElement`.\nPositive index → singleton monomial.\nNegative index → Hecke inverse.\n\nRequires `[NeZero n]` so that `_ % n < n` is well-defined. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.hecke_inverse_eq_sub","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.hecke_inverse_eq_sub","kind":"theorem","line":719,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeGS.lean#L719-L727","doc":"**The corrected inverse is an inverse.** In any ring, an element `x`\nsatisfying the Hecke quadratic `x² = h·x + 1` with `h` commuting with `x`\nis invertible with inverse `x - h`. With `h = q - q⁻¹` this is the formula\n`embedNegativeGen` encodes. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.embedNegativeGen","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.embedNegativeGen","kind":"def","line":701,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeGS.lean#L701-L717","doc":"Embed a negative generator `σᵢ⁻¹` via the Hecke relation inverse:\n`σᵢ⁻¹ = σᵢ - (q - q⁻¹)`.\n\nDerived from `σᵢ² = (q-q⁻¹)σᵢ + 1`: multiplying by `σᵢ⁻¹` gives\n`σᵢ = (q-q⁻¹) + σᵢ⁻¹`, i.e. the skein relation `σᵢ - σᵢ⁻¹ = q - q⁻¹`.\nCheck: `σᵢ(σᵢ - (q-q⁻¹)) = σᵢ² - (q-q⁻¹)σᵢ = 1`.\n\n**Corrected 2026-11-15 (bean `qou-078y`).** This read\n`σᵢ⁻¹ = (q⁻¹ - q)σᵢ + q⁻¹`, whose product with `σᵢ` is\n`(q⁻¹-q)(q-q⁻¹)σᵢ + (q⁻¹-q) + q⁻¹σᵢ`, which is not `1` for any `q ≠ ±1`\n(at `q = 2` it is `-(5/4)σᵢ - 3/2`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.embedPositiveGen","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.embedPositiveGen","kind":"def","line":696,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeGS.lean#L696-L699","doc":"Embed a positive generator `σᵢ` as the singleton monomial `[σᵢ]`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.dist_algebra_gs_basis_false","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.dist_algebra_gs_basis_false","kind":"theorem","line":680,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeGS.lean#L680-L692","doc":"**The former axiom `dist_algebra_gs_basis` is false.**\n\nIt asserted that every rewriting system over every field is a\nGröbner–Shirshov basis (its `DistAlgGenerators` argument was unused).\nThe Hecke system at `n = 4` refutes it. The axiom was deleted from\n`UGB.GrobnerShirshov.NormalForms`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.hecke_is_gs_basis_false","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.hecke_is_gs_basis_false","kind":"theorem","line":666,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeGS.lean#L666-L678","doc":"**The former axiom `hecke_is_gs_basis` is false.**\n\nIt asserted `∀ n (hn : 0 < n) (hp : HeckeParams), IsGrobnerShirshovBasis …` for\n`heckeRewritingSystem`; `n = 4` refutes it. The axiom has been deleted from\nthis file: with the repaired definitions it would have made the library\ninconsistent, not merely optimistic. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.NotAGSBasis.hecke_not_gs_basis_four","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.NotAGSBasis.hecke_not_gs_basis_four","kind":"theorem","line":651,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeGS.lean#L651-L662","doc":"**The Hecke relations are not a Gröbner–Shirshov basis at `n = 4`.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.NotAGSBasis.spoly_isNormalForm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.NotAGSBasis.spoly_isNormalForm","kind":"theorem","line":642,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeGS.lean#L642-L649","doc":"The S-polynomial is a normal form. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.NotAGSBasis.no_rule_infix_w₂","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.NotAGSBasis.no_rule_infix_w₂","kind":"theorem","line":632,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeGS.lean#L632-L640","doc":"No rule of the system applies to `σ₃σ₂σ₁σ₃`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.NotAGSBasis.no_rule_infix_w₁","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.NotAGSBasis.no_rule_infix_w₁","kind":"theorem","line":622,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeGS.lean#L622-L630","doc":"No rule of the system applies to `σ₂σ₃σ₂σ₁`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.NotAGSBasis.no_fc_infix_w₂","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.NotAGSBasis.no_fc_infix_w₂","kind":"theorem","line":619,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeGS.lean#L619-L620","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.NotAGSBasis.no_yb_infix_w₂","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.NotAGSBasis.no_yb_infix_w₂","kind":"theorem","line":616,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeGS.lean#L616-L617","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.NotAGSBasis.no_sq_infix_w₂","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.NotAGSBasis.no_sq_infix_w₂","kind":"theorem","line":613,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeGS.lean#L613-L614","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.NotAGSBasis.no_fc_infix_w₁","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.NotAGSBasis.no_fc_infix_w₁","kind":"theorem","line":610,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeGS.lean#L610-L611","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.NotAGSBasis.no_yb_infix_w₁","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.NotAGSBasis.no_yb_infix_w₁","kind":"theorem","line":607,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeGS.lean#L607-L608","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.NotAGSBasis.no_sq_infix_w₁","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.NotAGSBasis.no_sq_infix_w₁","kind":"theorem","line":604,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeGS.lean#L604-L605","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.NotAGSBasis.spoly_support","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.NotAGSBasis.spoly_support","kind":"theorem","line":570,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeGS.lean#L570-L597","doc":"Everything the S-polynomial is supported on is one of three words. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.NotAGSBasis.spoly_coeff_w₁","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.NotAGSBasis.spoly_coeff_w₁","kind":"theorem","line":557,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeGS.lean#L557-L568","doc":"The S-polynomial has coefficient `1` at `σ₂σ₃σ₂σ₁`: it is not zero. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.NotAGSBasis.fc_lc","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.NotAGSBasis.fc_lc","kind":"theorem","line":552,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeGS.lean#L552-L555","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.NotAGSBasis.yb_lc","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.NotAGSBasis.yb_lc","kind":"theorem","line":547,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeGS.lean#L547-L550","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.NotAGSBasis.w₂","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.NotAGSBasis.w₂","kind":"def","line":545,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeGS.lean#L545-L545","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.NotAGSBasis.w₁","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.NotAGSBasis.w₁","kind":"def","line":543,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeGS.lean#L543-L544","doc":"The two irreducible words the S-polynomial is supported on. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.NotAGSBasis.fc_mem","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.NotAGSBasis.fc_mem","kind":"theorem","line":537,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeGS.lean#L537-L541","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.NotAGSBasis.yb_mem","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.NotAGSBasis.yb_mem","kind":"theorem","line":531,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeGS.lean#L531-L535","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.NotAGSBasis.oc","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.NotAGSBasis.oc","kind":"def","line":520,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeGS.lean#L520-L529","doc":"The overlap composition on the ambient word `σ₃σ₂σ₃σ₁`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.NotAGSBasis.fc_lm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.NotAGSBasis.fc_lm","kind":"theorem","line":517,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeGS.lean#L517-L518","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.NotAGSBasis.yb_lm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.NotAGSBasis.yb_lm","kind":"theorem","line":514,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeGS.lean#L514-L515","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.NotAGSBasis.fc","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.NotAGSBasis.fc","kind":"def","line":511,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeGS.lean#L511-L512","doc":"The far-commutation rule for `(σ₃, σ₁)`; `lm = σ₃σ₁`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.NotAGSBasis.yb","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.NotAGSBasis.yb","kind":"def","line":508,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeGS.lean#L508-L509","doc":"The Yang–Baxter rule for the adjacent pair `(σ₂, σ₃)`; `lm = σ₃σ₂σ₃`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.NotAGSBasis.hn4","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.NotAGSBasis.hn4","kind":"theorem","line":505,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeGS.lean#L505-L506","doc":"`0 < 4`, once, so that every statement below is about the same system. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.one_isNormalForm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.one_isNormalForm","kind":"theorem","line":469,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeGS.lean#L469-L474","doc":"The unit is in normal form for the Hecke system. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.one_does_not_reduce_to_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.one_does_not_reduce_to_zero","kind":"theorem","line":459,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeGS.lean#L459-L467","doc":"**The unit does not reduce to zero.**  This is the acceptance test for the\nthree repairs of `Basic.lean` (bean qou-auq3): under the old definitions\nevery element reduced to zero, so `IsGrobnerShirshovBasis` was satisfied by\nevery rewriting system whatsoever. It is not any more. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.gs_basis_of_empty_lm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.gs_basis_of_empty_lm","kind":"theorem","line":331,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeGS.lean#L331-L455","doc":"**A rule that is a non-zero scalar collapses the GS property.**\n\nIf some rule's leading monomial is `[]` and its constant term is invertible —\nwhich is exactly what the removed sentinel `⟨ofTerms [([], q)], _⟩` was — then\n*every* element of the free algebra reduces to zero and\n`IsGrobnerShirshovBasis` holds for any generators, any order, any rules. The\npredicate then distinguishes nothing.\n\nTwo remarks on the statement, relative to the version proved against the\n*unrepaired* definitions:\n\n* the hypothesis `lc ≠ 0` is new and is needed. Previously\n  `SingleStepReduction` imposed no algebraic condition, so a rule with empty\n  leading monomial rewrote anything to anything; now a step must subtract an\n  actual multiple of the relation, and a relation with vanishing constant term\n  subtracts nothing. The removed sentinel satisfies it (`q > 0`).\n* the support hypothesis one might expect — that the relation is supported on\n  `[]` alone — is *not* needed: `AdmissibleOrder.not_lt_nil` shows the empty\n  word is the minimum of every admissible order, so a relation whose leading\n  monomial is `[]` has no other monomials at all. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.heckeRewritingSystem_lm_ne_nil","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.heckeRewritingSystem_lm_ne_nil","kind":"theorem","line":321,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeGS.lean#L321-L327","doc":"No rule of the Hecke system has an empty leading monomial. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.heckeRewritingSystem_lm_cases","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.heckeRewritingSystem_lm_cases","kind":"theorem","line":307,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeGS.lean#L307-L319","doc":"Every rule of `heckeRewritingSystem` is one of the three families, and its\nleading monomial is the explicit word listed here. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.mem_heckeRewritingSystem_rules","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.mem_heckeRewritingSystem_rules","kind":"theorem","line":282,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeGS.lean#L282-L305","doc":"**Every rule of `heckeRewritingSystem` is one of the three relations**, with\nits indices and its side condition. This is the inversion of the three `_mem`\nlemmas, and unlike `heckeRewritingSystem_lm_cases` it lands on the rule itself,\nwhich is what any statement about `spoly` needs. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.farCommRelation_lm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.farCommRelation_lm","kind":"theorem","line":253,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeGS.lean#L253-L263","doc":"`lm(σᵢσⱼ − σⱼσᵢ) = [σᵢ, σⱼ]` when `j < i`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.yangBaxterRelation_lm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.yangBaxterRelation_lm","kind":"theorem","line":240,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeGS.lean#L240-L251","doc":"`lm(σᵢσⱼσᵢ − σⱼσᵢσⱼ) = [σⱼ, σᵢ, σⱼ]` when `i < j` — the *reverse* of the\norientation claimed by `yangBaxterRelation`'s docstring. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.heckeRelation_lm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.heckeRelation_lm","kind":"theorem","line":228,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeGS.lean#L228-L238","doc":"`lm(σᵢ² − (q−q⁻¹)σᵢ − 1) = [σᵢ, σᵢ]`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.heckeOrder_lt_of_lex","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.heckeOrder_lt_of_lex","kind":"theorem","line":222,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeGS.lean#L222-L226","doc":"Equal-length words compare lexicographically by generator rank. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.heckeOrder_lt_of_length","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.heckeOrder_lt_of_length","kind":"theorem","line":218,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeGS.lean#L218-L220","doc":"Shorter words are smaller in the deg-lex order. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.heckeRewritingSystem","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.heckeRewritingSystem","kind":"def","line":158,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeGS.lean#L158-L189","doc":"The complete Hecke rewriting system for `H_n(q)`.\nCollects all Hecke, Yang–Baxter, and far-commutativity relations\nfor generators `σ₀, …, σ_{n-1}`.\n\n**Requires `0 < n`, and carries no sentinel rule.** An earlier version\nappended `⟨ofTerms [([], q)], _⟩` to satisfy `RewritingSystem.nonempty` at\n`n = 0`. That rule's support is `{[]}`, so its leading monomial is the empty\nword, and `[] <:+: m` holds for every `m` — which made `isNormalForm` false\nfor every element with non-empty support and collapsed the whole GS property\n(`gs_basis_of_empty_lm` below proves the collapse). With `0 < n` the Hecke\nrelation for `σ₀` supplies the non-emptiness instead, and every leading\nmonomial is a genuine word. `n = 0` is no loss: `H_0(q)` has no generators. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.farCommRelation","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.farCommRelation","kind":"def","line":147,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeGS.lean#L147-L156","doc":"The far-commutativity relation for non-adjacent generators:\n`σᵢσⱼ - σⱼσᵢ = 0` when `|i-j| ≥ 2`, oriented so that the\nhigher-index generator comes first (lm = `[σᵢ, σⱼ]` with `i > j`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.yangBaxterRelation","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.yangBaxterRelation","kind":"def","line":136,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeGS.lean#L136-L145","doc":"The Yang–Baxter relation for adjacent generators `σᵢ, σᵢ₊₁`:\n`σᵢσᵢ₊₁σᵢ - σᵢ₊₁σᵢσᵢ₊₁ = 0`, oriented as\n`σᵢσᵢ₊₁σᵢ → σᵢ₊₁σᵢσᵢ₊₁`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.heckeRelation","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.heckeRelation","kind":"def","line":120,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeGS.lean#L120-L134","doc":"The Hecke relation for generator `σᵢ`:\n`σᵢ² - (q - q⁻¹)σᵢ - 1 = 0`, oriented as\n`σᵢ² → (q - q⁻¹)σᵢ + 1`.\n\nAs an `AlgElement`: leading monomial `[σᵢ, σᵢ]` with coefficient 1,\nplus `[σᵢ]` with coefficient `-(q - q⁻¹)`, plus `[]` with\ncoefficient `-1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.HeckeParams.q_ne_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.HeckeParams.q_ne_one","kind":"theorem","line":116,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeGS.lean#L116-L116","doc":"`q ≠ 1` (non-classical). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.HeckeParams.q_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.HeckeParams.q_pos","kind":"theorem","line":114,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeGS.lean#L114-L114","doc":"`q > 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.HeckeParams.q","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.HeckeParams.q","kind":"def","line":112,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeGS.lean#L112-L112","doc":"The deformation parameter `q`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.HeckeParams.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.HeckeParams.mk","kind":"ctor","line":110,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeGS.lean#L110-L110","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.HeckeParams","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.HeckeParams","kind":"structure","line":109,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeGS.lean#L109-L116","doc":"Deformation parameter for the Hecke algebra. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.heckeOrder","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.heckeOrder","kind":"def","line":100,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeGS.lean#L100-L105","doc":"The deg-lex admissible order on Hecke monomials.\nConstructed via the generic `mkDegLexOrder` from AlgOps.lean,\nreusing the same proof infrastructure as `degLexOrder` for\n`SU2Gen` in NormalForms.lean. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.HeckeGen.rank_injective","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.HeckeGen.rank_injective","kind":"theorem","line":93,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeGS.lean#L93-L98","doc":"The rank function for `HeckeGen n` is injective. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.σ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.σ","kind":"def","line":87,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeGS.lean#L87-L89","doc":"Shorthand: create a Hecke generator from a natural number index.\nReturns the generator `σ_i` when `i < n`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.HeckeGen.rank","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.HeckeGen.rank","kind":"def","line":84,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeGS.lean#L84-L85","doc":"The rank of a Hecke generator (for deg-lex ordering). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.instDecidableEqHeckeGen.decEq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.instDecidableEqHeckeGen.decEq","kind":"def","line":82,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeGS.lean#L82-L82","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.instDecidableEqHeckeGen","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.instDecidableEqHeckeGen","kind":"instance","line":82,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeGS.lean#L82-L82","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.HeckeGen.index","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.HeckeGen.index","kind":"def","line":81,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeGS.lean#L81-L81","doc":"Generator index (0-based). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.HeckeGen.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.HeckeGen.mk","kind":"ctor","line":79,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeGS.lean#L79-L79","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.HeckeGen","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.HeckeGen","kind":"structure","line":77,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeGS.lean#L77-L82","doc":"Generator type for the Hecke algebra `H_n(q)`.\nFor `n` strands, there are `n` generators `σ₀,…,σ_{n-1}`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}